    {
      "id": "antony-and-cleopatra/sceneI_3.4/p@31787",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "CAESAR.\nYou may see, Lepidus, and henceforth know,\nIt is not Caesar’s natural vice to hate\nOur great competitor. From Alexandria\nThis is the news: he fishes, drinks, and wastes\nThe lamps of night in revel: is not more manlike\nThan Cleopatra, nor the queen of Ptolemy\nMore womanly than he; hardly gave audience, or\nVouchsafed to think he had partners. You shall find there\nA man who is the abstract of all faults\nThat all men follow.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
